### hilavitkutin-conformance

The instruments a runner of work units is held to. A one-thread reference
runner, `Oracle`, that states what a frame means and takes value-form units
through `RecordOp::apply` alone; a digest, `Fold`, that writes a frame's stores
down as one word, the same on every target; and the laws, functions over
recorded runs that return a `Verdict` naming where a law first failed. The
mutants each law has to fail ship beside the faithful runner. `no_std`, no
alloc. Depends on `hilavitkutin-api` and the foundations, never on the engine;
the engine's own suite and `hilavitkutin-frozen-authors` use it in their tests.
